<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>The Fighter-Bomber Aviation Regiment, 1987</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;IMG src="http://modelsua.com/images/D/ARTM7214_1.jpg"&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;0500L, 10 January 1987&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;After a long, cold&amp;nbsp;night dealing with a snap combat preparedness alert, your g-suit is starting to become uncomfortable. As you look&amp;nbsp;over yet another maintenance memorandum from your regimental aviation-technical officer, an armed courier escorted by two military policemen&amp;nbsp;appears at your regimental headquarters.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;"Comrade Colonel. Priority packet from Division headquarters."&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Overhearing, your suddenly wide-eyed &lt;EM&gt;zampolit &lt;/EM&gt;(political officer)&amp;nbsp;joins you. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;EM&gt;He knows something&lt;/EM&gt;. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;You open the heavy sealed envelope. Orders, maps, and a personal memo from the Aviation Division commander spill out onto the table already thick with half-eaten black bread and mugs of lukewarm tea.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;You have one hour to&amp;nbsp;prepare your first airstrike of the war.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;////////////&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Inspiration and detail provided by he excellent book &lt;U&gt;Soviet Tactical Aviation&lt;/U&gt;, authored by Yefim Gordon and Dmitry Komissarov. Hiroki Publications, 2011. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;-Scenario by Hellfish6&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;13 Dec 14&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
